  "interpretation": "The cumulative path-length fraction is a monotonic, label-free progress target. Its cross-trial spread quantifies why a fixed frame-index decoder averages motion. V10 should predict progress from CSI and query a global action motion bank; it should not reinterpret these quantiles as impact or injury labels. Static trials must be gated out because their apparent progress is dominated by GVHMR jitter."
